---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
const path = '/alternatives/smsbump-alternative';
const title = 'SMSBump alternatives: replace a retired Shopify SMS service';
const desc = 'Choose a current SMS destination from surviving SMSBump records, demonstrate sender and workflow continuity, and compare a matched replacement quote.';
const faqs = [
  { question: 'Can I keep buying SMSBump?', answer: 'No new purchase should be planned around the retired service. The current Yotpo SMS notice says its dashboard and background services are inactive.' },
  { question: 'Which alternatives did Yotpo name?', answer: 'Yotpo named Attentive and Omnisend in its 2025 migration announcement. Ask for current scope and terms; this is not an independent performance ranking.' },
  { question: 'Does Sequenzy replace the SMS sender?', answer: 'Keeping Sequenzy for email can be a separate decision. Require a current SMS destination and a demonstrated coordination process rather than assuming email capability replaces SMS.' },
  { question: 'Can I import every old number?', answer: 'Reconcile original permission evidence and current withdrawals. Keep unresolved records outside sendable audiences; an import date or purchase does not establish SMS eligibility.' },
  { question: 'Will my old number transfer?', answer: 'Have the destination confirm registration, ownership, transfer feasibility and reply routing in writing. An imported contact list does not transfer sender identity.' },
  { question: 'Which replacement costs least?', answer: 'Obtain matched ordinary and peak-month quotes including segments, destinations, carrier fees, services, staffing and contract commitments. No universal price winner is established here.' },
  { question: 'Should I replace email too?', answer: 'Keep a functioning email platform if it meets the requirements. Demonstrate preference propagation, purchase cancellation and flow ownership across senders before activation.' },
  { question: 'When is cutover complete?', answer: 'When required workflows pass, old queues and integrations are disabled, customer instructions work, and current owners can explain eligibility, replies and failures. Use readiness evidence rather than a fixed overlap period.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/alternatives">← Alternatives</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Legacy SMS replacement · checked November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Replace SMSBump without losing the meaning of your records</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">An old SMSBump list is a starting inventory, not a working replacement program. Choose a current sender that can explain which records are eligible, reproduce the jobs you still need and give an operator control over failures. There is no supported universal winner or savings figure for that handoff.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>The old service is retired</h2>
      <p>Yotpo's <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">2025 migration announcement</a> scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current notice</a> confirms that the SMS dashboard and background services are inactive. Do not plan a new SMSBump subscription or promise a live-dashboard export.</p>
      <p>For name history and a provenance ledger, use the <a class="link" href="/apps/smsbump">SMSBump record-continuity guide</a>. This page turns that inventory into a destination brief. If the project also includes Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty, the <a class="link" href="/alternatives/yotpo-email-sms-alternative">wider module replacement guide</a> covers those separate decisions.</p>
      <p>First inspect any replacement already installed. Reimporting an archive can reintroduce people who subsequently withdrew. Keep the archive's capture date, original permission evidence and current destination status distinct; ask support what missing records remain recoverable rather than inventing their history.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8 overflow-x-auto">
      <h2>Build a shortlist from the gap you actually have</h2>
      <p>Yotpo named Attentive and Omnisend as migration partners in 2025. That is a supplier recommendation, not an independent ranking or proof that historical assistance and offers remain available. Request current terms and an account-specific demonstration.</p>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Replacement job</th><th>Candidate route</th><th>Required proof</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Replace SMS while keeping working email</td><td>Compare a proposal from Attentive or Omnisend with an SMS-focused candidate such as Postscript</td><td>Sender setup, destination coverage, existing email coordination and staffed replies</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rebuild both channels</td><td>Request both channels in the named partners' proposals</td><td>Your email templates, events and audiences as well as SMS; one price for the complete workload</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keep an existing email platform</td><td>Retain Sequenzy, Klaviyo or another current sender if it meets the brief</td><td>A working preference and cancellation bridge; email capability alone does not replace SMS</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Use Reviews or Loyalty data in texts</td><td>Include retained module owners in procurement</td><td>Actual fields, identity matching, refresh behavior and request ownership in the destination</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Use the <a class="link" href="/apps/attentive">Attentive acquisition and operations review</a>, <a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend guide</a> and <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript guide</a> to prepare questions. Their inclusion here is not a feature guarantee or an ordered recommendation. Do not discard a functioning email program just to recreate a former bundle.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Give every candidate the same continuity packet</h2>
      <p>Provide a small redacted sample of eligible, withdrawn, duplicate and unresolved records. Include source identifiers, timestamps, purpose, sender history and the latest known exclusions. Ask the candidate to explain each import decision and preserve the audit trail. A contact count that matches the old CSV is insufficient.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Sender identity:</strong> obtain written confirmation of whether the old number can transfer, who owns registration and what customers should use for replies. If transfer is unavailable, document new signup instructions and remove obsolete keyword promotions.</li>
        <li><strong>Cart and inventory:</strong> reproduce one cart job with a known SKU. Change stock, purchase and permission on separate test profiles before dispatch; inspect cancellation and prevent duplicates when the event is replayed.</li>
        <li><strong>Offers and segments:</strong> import a VIP segment as a historical snapshot, then demonstrate a live qualification rule. Remove eligibility after a return or tier change and verify that an expired coupon cannot survive in a queued text.</li>
        <li><strong>Customer replies:</strong> send a sizing question, HELP and an opt-out through the proposed path. Assign an inbox owner and escalation cover, and demonstrate how withdrawals reach every sending system.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>These are proposed acceptance exercises, not merchant tests we observed. Record configuration, evidence, owner and pass/fail for each. Missing permission or a failed cancellation blocks the affected flow; extra templates cannot compensate for it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Price the replacement workload, including peak season</h2>
      <p>Use your destinations, encoding, SMS segments, MMS requirements, automations and campaign volume. Ask how undelivered messages, carrier fees, minimum commitments, number registration and support are charged. Price ordinary and peak months separately and include contract overlap, integration work and reply staffing. A headline subscription price cannot establish the cheaper replacement.</p>
      <p>Keep discount and fulfillment costs beside messaging cost. An illustrative order with $60 net receipts after discounts, $25 goods cost, $8 fulfillment and $2 messaging leaves $25 before fixed costs. This is arithmetic, not an observed SMSBump result. Estimate incremental contribution using a suitable eligible comparison group; a platform-attributed order may have happened without a text.</p>
      <p>Specify your own interruption policy across channels. Let email carry education and product context when appropriate, and reserve SMS for a justified timely message. Do not use an unopened email as permission or impose an invented universal twenty-four-hour gap. At dispatch check current permission, exclusions, purchase state and the chosen contact policy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Accept the destination and retire leftover instructions</h2>
      <p>Activate only the flows that passed. Record the current preference source, sender, reply owner, event source, duplicate key and cancellation owner. Confirm replaced jobs are disabled, remove old widgets and webhook subscriptions, and check customer-facing signup links on the devices you use. Preserve billing closure and unavailable-record notes.</p>
      <p>After launch inspect delivery failures, queued jobs, opt-outs by flow and reply backlog against the documented baseline. Schedule follow-up around actual workload and issues rather than an arbitrary migration duration. If a required flow fails, pause that flow and resolve its owner or data gap before expanding campaigns.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="SMSBump replacement FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
